## Structure

| Path | Role | May import |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `{{ module }}.py` | Domain entity and its rules | nothing from the framework |
| `use_cases/` | One file per capability | the domain, the repository interface |
| `storage.py` | SQLAlchemy model and repository | SQLAlchemy, the domain |
| `http.py` | Router and wire schemas | FastAPI, the use cases |
| `public.py` | The only file other modules may import. Takes a session and `tenant_id`, returns DTOs | storage, the use cases, the domain |

The import direction only ever points inward: `http` knows `use_cases`,
`use_cases` knows the domain, and the domain knows nothing.

## Use cases

| File | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `create_{{ module }}.py` | Validate through the entity, reject duplicates, persist |
| `list_{{ module }}.py` | Paginated listing with a capped page size |
| `get_{{ module }}.py` | Fetch one or raise `NotFoundError` |
| `update_{{ module }}.py` | Partial update, re-validated against merged state |
| `delete_{{ module }}.py` | Remove one |

Adding a capability means adding a file here. It does not mean growing a
service class until nobody can find anything in it.

